-- title:
--   Residue field of a completed two-variable chart via constant coefficients
-- statement:
--   Let $B_0$ be a commutative ring and $\mathfrak m_0 \subset B_0$ a maximal ideal, let $W_0$ be a local commutative ring, let $g_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ be a formal power series in two variables whose constant coefficient lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, and let $e_0$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_0$-adic completion $\widehat{(B_0)}_{\mathfrak m_0}$ onto $W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(g_0)$. Then there exists a ring homomorphism $\rho \colon B_0 \to \kappa(W_0)$ into the residue field of $W_0$ such that: $\rho$ is surjective; $\ker \rho = \mathfrak m_0$; and $\rho$ reads constants off the chart in the following sense: for all $b \in B_0$ and $w \in W_0$, if the difference of $e_0$ applied to the image of $b$ under the structure map $B_0 \to \widehat{(B_0)}_{\mathfrak m_0}$ and the class of the constant series $C(w)$ lies in the image under $W_0[[X_0,X_1]] \to W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(g_0)$ of the ideal $(X_0, X_1) + \mathfrak m_{W_0} \cdot W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ (more precisely, the join of the span of $X_0, X_1$ with the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ under $C$), then $\rho(b)$ equals the residue class of $w$.
--
--   The statement identifies the residue field $B_0/\mathfrak m_0$ of the point with the residue field $\kappa(W_0)$ of the coefficient ring, compatibly with a chart presenting the completed local ring as a hypersurface quotient of a two-variable power series ring, and records the congruence rule by which the identification is computed. It is used in the construction of ring isomorphisms between adic completions of stalks of Drinfeld charts on full-level modular curves after base change.
